      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] ❌ **Changes Requested** — Missing explicit padding, a minor commit message typo, and an unrelated bundled change require resolution.\n\n### Review Summary\n* **Functionality:** The newly introduced commands and telemetry event properly support power monitoring declarations.\n* **Architecture \u0026 Component Fit:** The structures are placed correctly in `ec_commands.h`. However, the CL inadvertently bundles the `EC_FEATURE_CONSOLE_LOG_EVENT` feature flag into `ec_features.c`, which is strictly unrelated to Power Monitoring.\n* **Code Simplicity:** Good, but explicit padding must be added.\n* **Idiomaticity \u0026 Readability:** Struct declarations violate the `__ec_todo_packed` rule. `__ec_todo_packed` is exclusively reserved for grandfathered structs, and MUST NOT be used in new code.\n* **Security:** Adding explicit padding is required to prevent the potential memory disclosure of uninitialized bytes sent over the wire.\n* **Testing \u0026 Test Coverage:** No dynamic logic is introduced in this CL since it is just interface declarations, so unit tests are not currently applicable here. Please ensure the follow-up implementation CL contains full automated test coverage.\n* **CL Size \u0026 Scope:** Size: M (+64, -0). The CL violates the Single Logical Change rule by bundling the unrelated `CONFIG_PLATFORM_EC_HOSTCMD_CONSOLE_EVENT`.\n* **Commit Message:** Includes minor typos (\"monitroing\" -\u003e \"monitoring\", \"subsystemm\" -\u003e \"subsystem\") but captures the core rationale well. `BUG\u003d` and `TEST\u003d` footers correctly match the Chromium convention.\n\nPlease see the inline comments for specific structural padding adjustments, formatting fixes, and the split request.\n[🔗](http://go/tj/cns/gg-d/home/tomhughes@google.com/review_trajectories/cl8279638_3f0ef6c2-e2a6-4a4c-979f-30ed1ca3d9a2.pb)",
